```toml meta
cacheable = true
role      = "a component a carrier wears: kernel-injectable TW5 module meme; capability gate for corpus-carried executable code"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme", "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapu"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tw5-module"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tw5-module"
```

!! TW5 Module Interface

A carrier that wears `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/tw5-module` declares its intent to supply a
kernel-injectable TW5 module. The boot gate `bootTrustedModules` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-module-gate.ts`)
queries for every carrier wearing this component (`stack:has`), admits only a carrier that this device preloaded at genesis and holds a LOCAL GRANT for, and adds each passing body as a JavaScript tiddler. `TW5Engine.boot` runs the gate in the host boot callback,
after TW5 completes its own module collection — so execution of a gated body during that boot reads UNBUILT.

!!! Required `#meta` Fields

| field | meaning |
|---|---|
| `content-type` | MUST read `"application/javascript"`; the built gate checks no such field and stamps the injected tiddler's `type` itself |
| `module-type` | the built gate admits `"library"` alone (an absent value reads as `"library"`) and refuses every other type by name: TW5 applies widget, filter and startup types during its own boot and never again |
| `tw5-module-name` | Proposed module registration key (e.g. `"text/memetic-wikitext"` for parsers); UNBUILT — the gate reads no such field, and TW5 registers a tiddler module under its `title` |
| `source-sha256` | tagged SHA-256 digest (`sha256:…`) of the module record's `text`; MUST match at inject time (gate layer 2 — content integrity); checked by `scripts/sync-heleuma.ts` during the build, which writes the field only under `--sync-modules --commit` |

!!! Body

The module record's `text` — what the deserializer yields for the carrier — MUST hold a self-contained CJS JS
bundle with no unresolved external imports. The bundle MAY reference `tiddlywiki` as the global `$tw` — the host
TW5 instance provides it at injection time. The gate skips an empty body.

!!! Capability Model

The kernel holds the `$tw.wiki` reference. Injecting a module meme into TW5 hands that reference
to the bundle's execution context. Three conditions must all hold before the kernel hands `$tw.wiki`
to any meme body:

# ''Local grant'' — the carrier appears in the promote ledger: a digest the device's own operator committed by hand, held on that device alone and not shadowed by a kāpae revocation. A field value on a carrier, however high or canonical-looking, grants nothing; a carrier without a grant fails closed.
# ''Content hash'' (`source-sha256` matches the tagged `sha256(text)`) — body integrity relative to the claimed digest, never authenticity or consent; checked by `scripts/sync-heleuma.ts` during `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build` and verified at inject time; a tampered or stale body fails here
# ''Module type'' — only `library` defines after boot; any other type refuses by name

The built gate skips a meme that lacks a grant or fails its digest or type check, and it executes no skipped body. A keyhive capability proof stays a possible further layer and reads UNBUILT. The grant stands on the device, so an offline wiki keeps every module it already promoted.

!!! Fallback

The gate carries no fallback of its own: when no module meme passes, it injects nothing. In the genesis
boot path the packed `lares-memetic-wikitext` plugin supplies the grammar, and TW5 collects its module
tiddlers natively. No `_registerMemeticParser()` and no `_registerWidgets()` stand in source.

